{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00372",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.91,
      "end_seconds": 4.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a few minutes behind, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.26,
      "end_seconds": 11.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.37,
      "end_seconds": 16.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "good morning, doctor i came along to help out"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.25,
      "end_seconds": 23.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 25.32,
      "end_seconds": 31.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Uh, doctor, it's an itchy rash. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.97,
      "end_seconds": 36.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "So, are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 37.97,
      "end_seconds": 54.47,
      "duration_seconds": 16.5,
      "text": "okay, so she is on Asthalin inhaler, when needed, I give it to to her uh, she takes hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema it's iron tablets, once a day for my blood count, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.25,
      "end_seconds": 57.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 58.74,
      "end_seconds": 68.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "For six months. She is on alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week for my bones, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.26,
      "end_seconds": 74.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "I, I used to take Seretide inhaler, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.33,
      "end_seconds": 79.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Right, since when have you had this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.38,
      "end_seconds": 90.94,
      "duration_seconds": 9.56,
      "text": "well, I'm not sure when it began, to to be honest some weeks ago, but I can't say how many"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.63,
      "end_seconds": 95.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Do you notice anything setting it off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.32,
      "end_seconds": 99.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Soap definitely sets it off"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.53,
      "end_seconds": 103.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Does anything make it better?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.62,
      "end_seconds": 107.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Moisturiser helps a bit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.73,
      "end_seconds": 113.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.96,
      "end_seconds": 118.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "A A seven out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.33,
      "end_seconds": 123.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Does it happen all the time or in spells?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.55,
      "end_seconds": 127.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "It just comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.99,
      "end_seconds": 135.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 135.88,
      "end_seconds": 141.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.86,
      "end_seconds": 151.62,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Okay, so there's itching that wakes me at night as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.89,
      "end_seconds": 157.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.43,
      "end_seconds": 167.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.46,
      "text": "Honestly, once or twice a day. Mild, I'd say. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.54,
      "end_seconds": 175.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "Have you had an itchy rash before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.17,
      "end_seconds": 183.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "A bit, about six months ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.85,
      "end_seconds": 188.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "any oozing, fever or new soap or detergent at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.57,
      "end_seconds": 204.77,
      "duration_seconds": 15.2,
      "text": "No, no oozing, no fever, no new soap or detergent. I did have cracked skin on my hands at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.34,
      "end_seconds": 214.58,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "Right, have you noticed similar rash in family members, breathing trouble or joint pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.64,
      "end_seconds": 218.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.04,
      "end_seconds": 225.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.29,
      "end_seconds": 230.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "right, you know, no, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.49,
      "end_seconds": 234.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "right, anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.01,
      "end_seconds": 236.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "no changes there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.09,
      "end_seconds": 239.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.14,
      "end_seconds": 245.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Hmm, I don't have any known medication allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.8,
      "end_seconds": 251.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.31,
      "end_seconds": 271.23,
      "duration_seconds": 18.92,
      "text": "I have asthma. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I just want to get back to normal, really. So, you know, I've had eczema, yes. I have low haemoglobin, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.93,
      "end_seconds": 272.83,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "go on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.35,
      "end_seconds": 278.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Well, I have thin bones, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.69,
      "end_seconds": 290.64,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Right, so so asthma and eczema are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. So, does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.62,
      "end_seconds": 294.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "I mean, my brother has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.9,
      "end_seconds": 298.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "And what do you usually eat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.73,
      "end_seconds": 304.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Mostly home-cooked food, rice and vegetables"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.59,
      "end_seconds": 308.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Let me measure a few things."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.51,
      "end_seconds": 322.31,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "one second.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.69,
      "end_seconds": 346.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.55,
      "text": "Okay: temp 36.6 degrees, pulse 76, blood pressure 108 over 72. And respiratory rate 15."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.7,
      "end_seconds": 349.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.44,
      "end_seconds": 354.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "So, that's fine, we'll come to to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.53,
      "end_seconds": 360.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "okay, I need to examine you for this"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.75,
      "end_seconds": 365.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "let me look at this properly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.18,
      "end_seconds": 387.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "There are dry red patches in the creases of both elbows with scratch marks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.4,
      "end_seconds": 391.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.26,
      "end_seconds": 412.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "No signs of infection, no crusting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 418.2,
      "end_seconds": 420.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Right, thanks for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 436.37,
      "end_seconds": 446.92,
      "duration_seconds": 10.55,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, the most likely explanation is an eczema flare-up. I'd also keep a fungal infection in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.5,
      "end_seconds": 451.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I mean, should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 452.02,
      "end_seconds": 458.58,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an eczema flare-up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 467.26,
      "end_seconds": 500.64,
      "duration_seconds": 33.38,
      "text": "You'll be taking cetirizine, 10 milligrams, at night, for one week. That's for itching. Let's use mometasone cream, once a day, for two weeks. It's for eczema. Moisturise right after a bath, thick creams are better than lotions, and use a mild soap. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. I'll want another look in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 501.49,
      "end_seconds": 503.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "sure, that's doable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 504.71,
      "end_seconds": 507.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 509.05,
      "end_seconds": 511.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. Bye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 512.08,
      "end_seconds": 513.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}